  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India, Basic Statistical Return 2: deposits with scheduled commercial banks including regional rural banks, annual, as on 31 March, and the quarterly return (from March 2023, excluding regional rural banks). Every BSR-2 table DBIE publishes: ownership (reports 737 and 1200), tables 1.2 to 1.5, 2.1 to 2.12, 3.1 to 3.8 and 4.1 to 4.2, annual and quarterly, and the 2010 to 2018 district table, read through the owner's local mirror of DBIE. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p>Checked against the RBI's own releases. March 2025: households held 60.2% of deposits and women 20.7%. March 2026 (release of 29 May 2026): households 59.3%, savings deposits 28.7%, term deposits 61.6%, senior citizens 20.0%, term deposits booked for one to three years 69.8%. These tables reproduce every one.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Amounts are converted from rupees to ₹ lakh crore (₹ crore in the deeper tables). The all-depositor total under the new classification is the sum of its five top-level sectors, which matches the published all-India figure. DBIE exports these tables without column titles; each column is named from RBI's table layout and proved by sums that must hold in every row (current, savings and term deposits add to the total; individuals and others to all depositors; the bank groups to all banks). The rows of percentages DBIE prints under each table (with a minus sign) are left out and recomputed. District totals are sums of a district's branches by population group. Nothing is estimated.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Two breaks are disclosed and never joined across: the change in sector classification between March 2018 and March 2019, and the finer deposit-size bands introduced in March 2026. The size chart uses the finer March 2026 bands only; the four older bands, with March 2026 summed into them, are in the data download.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.1 (October 2026), from RBI data to March 2026 (annual) and June 2026 (quarterly). v1.1 adds every BSR-2 table: owners one by one, age, states, districts, bank groups, staff, original maturity and the quarterly return. Revised each year when the RBI publishes the next return.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
